XSA_PLAN_V2_WITNESS witness stream = 8B x chi; chi/n = 0.283 is the 1GB FIXTURE ratio (the pile value is unmeasured): ~0 GB at this scale; if it exceeds --wit-ram-budget the overflow spills as sorted varint-delta disc runs (est. <= 0.3x raw, EXTRAPOLATED - unmeasured at spill scale) inside the tree
XSA_PLAN_V2_TRANSIENT no chunk set, no merge transient, no persistent position column: the producer's scratch is the piece window (0.036 GiB, W=1100 bands x 65536 runs), the rlebwt it is publishing (0.0 GiB) and the ROLLING WINDOW FILES (0.0 GiB on disc = 2 credit x cap x 8 B, one file per live window, unlinked the moment its bins are built); the build's RAM is one group (0.0 GiB, 16 B/slot) and NEVER the window; inputs the finish consumes are unlinked as read; witness spill reserve 0.0 GiB (0.3x overflow, EXTRAPOLATED)
XSA_PLAN_V2_CAP live_cap_slots=1200008 source=auto from --memory-gb 16 (bound by address space) bound_by=address space (--memory-gb): corpus cache + fill staging + 16 B/slot arena pair; MEMORY bound: 90% of --memory-gb 16 GiB (17179869184 B) = 15461882265 B usable - corpus cache 1200008 B (min(n, 512 B x pool slots 1048576)) - staging 167772160 B (4 threads x (33554432 B fill + 8388608 B leaf)) = 15292910097 B / 16 B per build-group slot = 955806881 slots; SCRATCH bound: 90% of 751.9 GiB free = 726590715494 B - rlebwt+pieces 40255468 B = 726550460026 B / (credit 2 x 8 B per slot) = 1200008 slots; window_file_gb=0.02 = credit x cap x 8 B ON DISC (0 B of address space: the fill writes with buffered pwrite, never a mapping); the finish is its own process under the same cap: witness 0.0 GiB fits it, headroom_pct=90
XSA_PLAN_V2_RAMSPLIT pool_gb=0.50 pool_share_of_memory_pct=3.1 pool_covers_corpus_pct=100.0 fill_stage_gb=0.12 leaf_stage_gb=0.03 arena_group_gb=14.24 finish_witness_gb=0.00 finish_pfck_grid_gb=0.00 usable_gb=14.40 rule=the pool is sized FIRST and pinned to the whole corpus text whenever --memory-gb allows (the hot set is the boilerplate epoch); the two staging buffers are constants per thread; the arena pair takes the remainder; the finish is a second process under the same cap and owns its witness stream + pfck grid
