XSA_PLAN_V2_TARGET rows=262144 leaves=5 levels_per_row=3.49 largest_leaf_rows<=262144 rule=subdivide-while-rows>target (depth is an OUTPUT of the census; the depth cap is a fail-loud backstop, not the rule)
XSA_PLAN_V2_POSITION_STORE window_file_gb=0.02 = credit(2) x cap(1200008) x 8 B ON DISC (one rolling file per live window, unlinked when built); ram_group_gb=0.02 = 16 B/slot x the group being sorted in place; position_io_gb=0.0 = 16 x n / (8+8) B a position written once and read once; position_io_s=0 at the 5.238 GB/s device floor (overlapped by the fill and the build, so not on the critical path); persistent_position_column=0 full_SA=0
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN_END e2e_s=0 e2e=0:00:00 producer=0:00:00 finish=0:00:00 rule=max(producer,finish) (concurrent, flow-controlled through the piece window)
XSA_PLAN_V2_BIN_NOTE 1 windows = ceil(n/1200008) (each window re-reads the whole corpus: fill = windows x n at the 5.238 GB/s device floor = 0.00 h at this scale); bins are indivisible so a window is packed to <= cap by whole bins (every measured point matches ceil exactly: 1 GB cap 250M -> 5, 1 GB cap>=n -> 1); a single bin larger than the cap makes the producer raise it (BIN_CAP_RAISED) and the front door FAILS LOUD rather than price a different arena. The TREE: 5 leaves = ceil(n/target), each a comparison sort of <= 262144 rows (depth is an OUTPUT of the byte census; mean levels/row 3.49 measured at this target, i.e. the emergent depth is 0 for the busiest bucket, not a parameter). Terms (s/GB at 1 GB): count 1.360 fill 0.191+0.191/window build 107.930@4t stitch 11.408 = producer 120.89; finish 118.90 (own work); e2e = max = 120.89. Measured 1 GB producer wall 41.68 s and with-finish 142.18 s (flow-limited): the model holds the producer term to 290.0%
